From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 21:52:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 100/117] media: iris: give picture-less capture buffers back
 to the firmware

The decoder firmware also returns capture buffers it consumed without
producing a picture (reference-only use, data_size 0, no timestamp),
about 1.5 returns per decoded frame on AV1. The driver hands each of them
to the client as a V4L2_BUF_FLAG_ERROR frame, so every client pays a
dequeue / queue round trip per return: GStreamer drops and requeues them
with its "Decoder is producing too many buffers" warning, and ffmpeg's
v4l2m2m wrapper counts them as decoded frames.

While streaming, queue such a buffer to the firmware again with the
helper already used for hidden reference pictures, so clients only see
real pictures. At drain (the last buffer, or the session no longer
streaming) and for buffers the firmware flagged as errors, they are
still returned to the client.

Found and measured by TheMojoMan (erhai iris tree 63e86475627f, "keep
picture-less capture buffers in the firmware", no Signed-off-by);
re-implemented on our requeue helper.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
---
 .../media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen2_response.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen2_response.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen2_response.c
index daaff08334b2f..704fb7db3ef1f 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen2_response.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen2_response.c
@@ -455,8 +455,19 @@ static int iris_hfi_gen2_handle_output_buffer(struct iris_inst *inst,
 			return iris_hfi_gen2_requeue_output_buffer(inst, buf);
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * The decoder also returns capture buffers it used without producing
+	 * a picture (about 1.5 per decoded frame on AV1). Returning them as
+	 * error frames costs every client a dequeue / queue round trip and
+	 * shows up as dropped or bogus frames (GStreamer "too many buffers",
+	 * ffmpeg counting them as frames). Give them back to the firmware, as
+	 * for hidden reference pictures above. At drain (the last buffer, or
+	 * not streaming any more) they are still returned to the client.
+	 */
 	if (!buf->data_size && inst->state == IRIS_INST_STREAMING &&
 	    !(buf->flags & V4L2_BUF_FLAG_LAST)) {
+		if (inst->domain == DECODER && !(buf->flags & V4L2_BUF_FLAG_ERROR))
+			return iris_hfi_gen2_requeue_output_buffer(inst, buf);
 		buf->flags |= V4L2_BUF_FLAG_ERROR;
 	}
 
